        <div class="tab-content" id="units-reference" role="tabpanel">
        <h2>📏 Supported Units Reference</h2>
        <p class="intro-text">
        Complete reference guide for all CSS properties in UtiliKit and their supported measurement units.
        Know exactly which units you can use with each property.
        </p>

        <div class="units-guide">
        <div class="quick-reference">
        <h3>Quick Unit Reference</h3>
        <div class="units-grid">
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>(none)</code> → <span>px (default)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>pr</code> → <span>% (percentage)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>em</code> → <span>em (relative to parent)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>rem</code> → <span>rem (relative to root)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>vh</code> → <span>vh (viewport height)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
        <code>vw</code> → <span>vw (viewport width)</span>
        </div>
        </div>
        </div>


